WEBVTT

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.850
<b>Sakura's Nostalgic Viewing Party</b>

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.300
You seem in a good mood today, Akiho-san.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.660
Was I being rude?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.730
No, I just noticed you 
smiling more than usual.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:26.060
I got to read more of the book!

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.920
Last time, a girl grew the 
ears and tail of a cat,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.510
but when Alice tried to tell her 
about it, they disappeared.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.080
I told you about that, right?

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:38.870
Yes.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:44.520
In the next part, all of Alice's friends 
turn into different animals.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.510
There's a bear, a squirrel, and even a sheep.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.770
That sounds fun.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.150
It was fun!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.780
I wonder what animal you would turn into.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.730
Huh?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.190
Well...

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.340
Perhaps a rabbit?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.270
I love rabbits!

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.700
What else was in the book?

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.950
The weather suddenly turned bad,

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.920
and the mood seemed really scary...

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:16.130
But Alice didn't give up and turned 
them all back to normal.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.260
That's nice.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:25.250
I hope Alice will continue to do her best.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.160
Kaito-san?

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.660
You're going out today, yes?

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:37.410
Yes, my friends invited me again!

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.180
I hope you have a wonderful day.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.520
Same to you!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.600
Go. Go.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.680
And now... What?!

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.320
Take this!

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.430
I did it!

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.590
Did ya see my driving technique?

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.350
Don't look in the mirror yet.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.700
I know, I know.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.720
So busy first thing in the morning, 
and on a weekend, no less...

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.010
There.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.840
It's done.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:15.120
Wh-What do you think? 
I've never tried this before...

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.170
I'd say it passes!

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.850
Oh, good!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:26.920
If you grew your hair out, I bet 
you could braid it yourself.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.050
You think so?

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.610
Have you always had that hairstyle?

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.940
Yeah. My dad cuts it for me.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.530
What?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.710
You don't get it cut at a salon?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:37.480
Nope.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.040
It's always been my dad.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.580
And lately, Yukito-san has been 
cutting my brother's hair.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.100
Who cuts your dad's hair?

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.020
My brother.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:45.840
What?!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.260
Do I want a V8 or a straight-eight engine?

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.530
No, maybe I should go for a 
straight-six to reduce weight...

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.600
Come to think of it, Syaoran's mom 
cut his hair when he was little.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.860
She said it was dangerous for 
a magic user to expose

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.410
their neck to any blades before 
they were strong enough.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:15.170
After that, he hated salons, 
so he had Wei cut it.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.900
Did he cut yours, too?

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.810
I always go to a salon!

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.160
I... I see!

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.560
Actually, I wonder what Syaoran 
does about his hair in Japan.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.400
What's wrong?

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.140
I was just wondering if 
Syaoran-kun is okay...

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.980
He sent you a message, didn't he?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:37.900
Yeah.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.010
But...

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.490
Written words don't tell you 
if he's really okay, huh?

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.130
Can't you just call him?

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.920
He might be sleeping.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.060
Then, I'll call him!

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.030
Huh?

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.130
Syaoran, zou san!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.650
Were you asleep?

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.350
Have you had breakfast?

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:12.050
You'll never get better if 
you don't eat, you know!

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.270
Yeah, Kinomoto-san did.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.280
Tell her that yourself.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:22.650
Huh?

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.080
He was awake.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:27.210
Here.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.720
H-Hello?

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:36.920
<i>Hello?</i>

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.610
I-It's Sakura.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:42.890
<i>Sorry I worried you. I'm perfectly fine now.</i>

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:44.930
Are you sure?

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:45.850
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.380
<i>I've been awake. I was just making breakfast.</i>

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.660
Make sure you eat well, okay?

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:56.310
And... Don't push yourself too hard.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:01.060
<i>I'm not.</i>

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.430
Okay.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.070
<i>Meiling isn't causing 
trouble for you, is she?</i>

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.600
Not at all. She's the one 
who's taking care of me.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:14.810
<i>She does like to look after people.</i>

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.670
<i>But people get the wrong idea 
because of how she talks.</i>

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:22.130
Hey! What're you doing?

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.360
She's really nice.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.290
<b>Sunday 
Meeting 
Akiho-chan 
at 9:00</b>

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.640
<i>You're going to Daidouji's 
place, today, right?</i>

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.690
You're in the way.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:24.730
You're in the way!

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.300
Yeah.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.800
<i>Sorry I can't make it, after you invited me.</i>

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.500
No, don't worry about it. 
Just rest as much as you can.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:35.630
Wow, this is pretty well 
made, for being so tiny.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.800
<i>Thanks. See you.</i>

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.620
Oh, hang on a second.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.150
Hey! Pay attention!

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.140
Never mind. See you later.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.870
See? He was fit as a fiddle.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:53.450
Yeah.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.070
Feel better now?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.900
Yeah! Thanks, Meiling-chan!

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.580
You're welcome.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:58.790
<b>Frog Cart 15</b>

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.030
But you know what, Kinomoto-san?

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:05.280
You worry far too much 
about the little things!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.910
You'd better get goin' soon, 
or you'll be late.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:09.800
Oh!

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.330
Akiho-chan!

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:17.600
Good morning, Sakura-san, Meiling-san.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.680
Morning.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:23.180
But are you sure you don't 
mind me coming along?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.910
You worry about that stuff, too?

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.600
Just like Kinomoto-san.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.310
Huh?

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.310
It's not a problem at all!

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:35.000
Daidouji-san is the one who said she 
wanted to show us something.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.070
And above all, I'm saying...

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.460
No problem! Right?

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.870
Thank you. That really makes me happy.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.790
You didn't understand that?

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.320
Pretty sure that was middle-school English...

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.440
Your pronunciation is too good!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.010
You're both amazing.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.820
Why don't you have Syaoran 
or Shinomoto-san help you?

00:08:58.820 --> 00:08:59.550
Huh?

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.730
I'll help, if you like!

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.560
Really? That'd be great!

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.630
These two are so alike.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:10.920
Yep, they sure are.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.900
<i>Please come in.</i>

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.670
This house looks as huge as ever!

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.870
I know. My first time here, it was so big,

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.390
I didn't even notice it.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.030
Excuse us—

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.550
Sakura-chan!

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:40.110
I'm so glad you're here.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:44.760
You're just as adorable as ever!

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:44.760
H-Hello.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.640
Are you off work, today, Sonomi-san?

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:54.900
I had all my meetings until 
this evening rescheduled.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.930
You were making all kinds 
of phone calls, yesterday.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:00.750
Yes!

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.420
Sakura-chan, Meiling-chan, and...

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.500
It's a pleasure to meet you, Akiho-chan.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.380
It's good to see you again.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.830
N-Nice to meet you. I'm Akiho Shinomoto.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:16.170
You must stay and have my 
handmade snacks for afternoon tea!

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.850
Akiho-chan, you've lived in England, right?

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:20.580
Yes.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.990
I hope you'll like my baking just as much!

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.620
<i>Yeah, yeah. Afternoon tea.</i>

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:26.970
Mother has been looking 
forward to your visit.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.010
Please make sure you eat some.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:33.370
Make yourselves at home 
until everything is ready.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:35.090
Thank you.

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:38.690
Afternoon tea... Afternoon tea!

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.530
Your mother is a lovely person, Tomoyo-san.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.980
Thank you.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.860
And powerful to boot!

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:48.330
Huh?

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.470
We're not going to your room?

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:52.830
Not today. I want to show you something.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.230
It's right this way.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.490
Wow!

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.750
Please help yourselves to the seats in front.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.870
Let's go, Shinomoto-san!

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:08.610
Okay.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.010
Is this where you watch movies and stuff?

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:13.650
Movies, too, but...

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.380
Mostly, I review my footage of you.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:19.650
Daidouji-san!

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:21.620
What's this?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.330
Go ahead and drink it.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.580
It's lemonade!

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:28.190
Yes!

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:30.260
It's so cute!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.590
So, what are we going to watch?

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:40.920
<b>At the Tomoeda Nadeshiko Festival 
Play: "Beautiful Romance" (0:48:39) 
Writer/Producer: Naoko Yanagisawa | Starring: Sakura Kinomoto</b>

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:45.930
<b>Nadeshiko Festival</b>

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:48.730
<i>The play presented by the students of Tomoeda 
Elementary School, Class 6-2, will now begin.</i>

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.610
I remember this!

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:52.180
I-Is this...

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.430
Akiho-chan, you said you 
wanted to see it, right?

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.430
T-Tomoyo-chan...

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:59.440
I'm in it, too!

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.660
What? But, but...

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:04.210
What's the problem? It's been 
ages. Let's watch it.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:08.280
Shinomoto-san, you should sit in the 
middle, since you haven't seen it.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:08.800
<i>Your Highness must be exhausted 
from fighting against</i>

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.160
Oh, are you sure?

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.870
<i>the neighboring country 
over the magic stone.</i>

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.700
Then, I'll take you up on that.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.450
<i>Everyone at this dance will wear masks.</i>

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:16.650
Sakura-chan, come sit here, 
next to Akiho-chan.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:17.400
<i>Please relax and enjoy the dance.</i>

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:22.100
Wow... This is amazing! Everyone is in it!

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:23.960
<i>Thank you. But I'm not a very good dancer.</i>

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:26.100
Daidouji-san made all of the costumes.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.370
<i>That's all right.</i>

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.970
<i>The best thing to do is find a dance 
partner who's a very good dancer.</i>

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.060
All of them?!

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:28.790
Yep.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.770
My acting really is incredible!

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.410
Yes, it is incredible!

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:38.560
Right? Isn't it?

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:43.810
Syaoran and I were actually back 
in Hong Kong, at the time.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:46.050
But we visited the school 
during summer break,

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.770
and they were practicing this 
play, so they put us in it.

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:51.730
Syaoran complained and 
said he wouldn't be in it,

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:54.630
but Yamazaki-kun got hurt, 
so he stood in for him!

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.330
I see...

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.940
Syaoran's acting got a lot better!

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:02.610
He played a princess in a play before 
this one, and he was awful.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.270
I'd love to see that one, next time.

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:08.940
<i>And it would be better if the magic stone 
that we've been fighting over</i>

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:14.460
<i>disappeared forever, 
rather than belong to anyone.</i>

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:15.530
<i>Absolutely.</i>

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.370
There's Syaoran!

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:21.630
<i>I feel the same way.</i>

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.640
<i>Who might you be?</i>

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.530
<i>We're not supposed to use names here.</i>

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.350
He learned all the lines and 
dance steps in one day.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:32.170
<i>That's right. This is the first 
masquerade ball I've ever been to.</i>

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:30.600
One day?

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.160
<i>Me, too.</i>

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:34.690
<i>My!</i>

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.660
He's too good.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:39.140
<i>Given my busy life, I had forgotten 
about the idea of dancing.</i>

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:39.460
He sounds so natural, 
it doesn't look like an act.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:44.620
It's as if he's saying what 
he means in his heart.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:44.430
<i>My retainers thought it would lift 
my spirits to come to this event.</i>

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.000
<i>It's the same with me.</i>

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.410
<i>We both hate war, and it's our 
first time attending a ball...</i>

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:48.420
<i>This is some kinda torment...</i>

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:50.260
<i>Hang in there, Sakura!</i>

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.550
<i>We're very much alike.</i>

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.820
<i>No, I can't say it.</i>

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.820
<i>This feeling I have for you...</i>

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.950
<i>No, I can't...</i>

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:06.450
<i>Please... I beg you. Please forget about me.</i>

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:10.140
<i>Please banish me from your heart.</i>

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.130
<i>Your Highness!</i>

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:13.420
Huh?

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.040
<b>Nadeshiko Festival 
Festival Day
 Play: "Beautiful Romance" 
Other</b>

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.030
There was an earthquake after that,

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:21.430
so the play couldn't be performed to the end.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.500
What?

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.980
Was anyone hurt?!

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:26.040
We were fine!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:30.550
I... I can't take anymore! I'm gonna 
die of embarrassment!

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:35.060
Don't be embarrassed! 
It was truly, truly wonderful!

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:39.620
Actually, this wasn't the only 
thing I wanted to show you.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.900
<b>Nadeshiko Festival 
Festival Day
 Play: "Beautiful Romance" 
Other</b>

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.650
<b>Rehearsal 
Rehearsal Day 1 
Rehearsal Day 2 
Rehearsal Day 3 
Rehearsal Day 4 
Morning Rehearsal Day 4 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 5 
Morning Rehearsal Day 5 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 6 
Morning Rehearsal Day 6 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 7 
Morning Rehearsal Day 7</b>

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:47.400
<i>But I'm not a very good dancer.</i>

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.180
<i>That's all right.</i>

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:56.230
<i>The best thing to do is find a dance 
partner who's a very good dancer.</i>

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:01.970
<i>And it would be better if the magic 
stone that we've been fighting over</i>

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:05.070
<i>disappeared forever, 
rather than belong to anyone.</i>

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.130
<i>Sorry, Sakura-chan.</i>

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:13.340
<i>Could you try saying, "Disappeared forever, 
rather than be in anyone's hands"?</i>

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.900
You really did film these?

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:18.680
Only occasionally, when the 
teacher said I could.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.540
So it's only bits and pieces.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:31.820
<b>Play starts at 7:30!    Be here at 6:00!</b>

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.270
<i>We'll have to practice the dancing part, too.</i>

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.920
<i>I'll have the teacher show me all the steps!</i>

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:31.830
<i>Sorry... It'd be best if I could 
teach you, but with this...</i>

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.680
<i>I learned the steps!</i>

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.030
<i>I also wrote it all down, just in case.</i>

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:38.760
<i>Thanks, Chiharu-chan.</i>

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:42.730
<i>Since Yamazaki-kun got hurt, 
it'll be rough for Li-kun.</i>

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:43.940
<i>It's the least I could do.</i>

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.610
<i>Don't laugh about this!</i>

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:49.600
<i>Okay, teach Li-kun the steps, please.</i>

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:53.480
<i>One, two, three. One, two, three...</i>

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:57.580
<i>Left, right, left, right, left, right...</i>

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.510
Sucks, doesn't he?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.270
But he quickly...

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:06.530
<i>One, two, three. One, two, three.</i>

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.580
<i>Okay, let's have you try 
it with the princess.</i>

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.060
<i>Sakura-chan!</i>

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.290
<i>R-Right.</i>

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.900
<i>Start from the moment you 
finish walking behind him!</i>

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.800
<i>Li-kun, you do this... And, 
Sakura-chan, you do this.</i>

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:27.520
<i>One, two, three... One, two...</i>

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.540
<i>Sorry!</i>

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.670
<i>No, I might have moved too fast.</i>

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.810
<i>Let's try again, slower.</i>

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.100
<i>O-Okay.</i>

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:41.090
<i>One, two, three... One, two, three...</i>

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:45.600
<i>One, two, three... One, two, three...</i>

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:50.110
<i>One, two, three... One, two, three...</i>

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:54.620
<i>One, two, three... One, two, three...</i>

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:59.110
<i>One, two, three... One, two, three...</i>

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.870
<i>One, two, three...</i>

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:18.780
<i>We did it!</i>

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:19.650
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.900
<i>That was great!</i>

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:26.610
<i>Syaoran, that was great! 
I barely recognized you!</i>

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.860
<b>Rehearsal 
Rehearsal Day 1 
Rehearsal Day 2 
Rehearsal Day 3 
Rehearsal Day 4 
Morning Rehearsal Day 4 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 5 
Morning Rehearsal Day 5 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 6 
Morning Rehearsal Day 6 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 7 
Morning Rehearsal Day 7</b>

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.350
Amazing.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:36.320
You really did practice your hardest!

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:39.390
It's so heartwarming!

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:42.120
Especially since they're both 
such serious people!

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.760
But, Daidouji-san, how many cameras 
did you have set up, anyway?

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:50.830
Sakura-san, you really are amazing!

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.960
I'd love to see this play through to the end!

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:59.490
Akiho-chan...

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.670
But of course!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.720
Li-kun is in Japan now, too.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:09.970
I would love to see you two 
acting again, so I can film—

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:13.610
So I can watch!

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:18.580
Naoko-chan did join the Theater Club, 
so we can make it happen!

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.940
Oh, that's right!

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:22.740
At that festival, Tomoyo-chan sang a solo.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:25.240
Wouldn't you like to see that, Akiho-chan?!

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:26.860
I would!

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:29.260
You sang, right, Tomoyo-chan? Right?

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:33.470
I did, but it wasn't that interesting.

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:34.740
I'd love to see it!

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.520
Enthusiasm gone!

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.050
<b>Rehearsal Day 5 
Morning Rehearsal Day 5 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 6 
Morning Rehearsal Day 6 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 7 
Morning Rehearsal Day 7 
Afternoon Rehearsal Day 8 
Morning Rehearsal Day 8 
Afternoon Amusement Park 
Rehearsal Day 9 
Morning Rehearsal Day 9 
Afternoon Festival Day</b>

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:40.260
<b>Song</b>

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:50.270
<b>Nadeshiko Festival</b>

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:54.410
You also made this costume yourself. 
Right, Daidouji-san?

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.900
This one, too?

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:57.570
Yes.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.400
It's so beautiful.

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:03.660
<b>Nadeshiko Festival</b>

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.040
It's starting!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:10.870
<i>The light of the setting sun 
paints the grasslands red.</i>

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.300
<i>Like burning fire.</i>

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:24.310
<i>The night sky is dotted with stars.</i>

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.310
<i>One by one.</i>

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:28.660
What's that?

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:39.160
Shinomoto-san?

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:40.700
It's too dangerous!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.020
But you gave it to me.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:43.720
Kero-chan...

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.680
This is no ordinary quake!

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:46.370
Yeah!

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:50.650
<i>Release!</i>

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:58.540
<i>Snooze!</i>

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:03.520
Hurry and get back in your seat!

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:04.210
O-Okay.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.130
Kinomoto-san!

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.640
Sakura, what do you feel? Is it in this room?

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.180
I don't think so.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.930
Hey, brat! Take over!

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.800
She's okay. I just put her 
to sleep with magic.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.290
Keep an eye on her.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:28.010
I know!

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.680
Tomoyo-chan, let's go find 
your mom and the others.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.000
Right!

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:36.490
Stay under the table.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.120
It's safer.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:40.610
Which way?

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:43.370
Go back the way we came! 
It's near the kitchen!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.760
Daidouji-san never changes...

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.190
Is the entire house shaking?

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.890
Tomoyo! Sakura-chan!

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.590
Are you all right?!

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.030
Yes! Are you?

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.490
We turned off all the lights!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.120
I've been told the electrical 
system is undamaged, too.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.030
Excuse me...

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.500
Is this everyone?

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:07.420
Yes...

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.740
Are you all right? And what about the others?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.450
I'm sorry.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:14.820
Sakura!

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:16.570
<i>Snooze!</i>

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:28.310
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! 
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:31.200
You never know when you'll need to use magic.

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:34.210
The house is still shaking. It's not safe.

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.190
Stay here, Tomoyo-chan.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:44.250
Of course. So you can do your job 
without worrying about me.

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:47.030
Kero-chan,

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.570
it's up to you!

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:50.370
Right, I got this!

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.220
I'll show ya just how hard I've trained!

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:57.190
<i>Flight!</i>

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.060
It seems very happy.

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:06.670
I guess it likes ya.

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:09.440
I'm counting on you, Flight-san.

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:12.970
Kero-chan!

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.020
Right!

00:24:10.020 --> 00:24:12.150
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.600
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.600
<b>K</b>

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:17.080
It's human nature to forget. We live in the 
moment. It's "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:20.060
Today, I'm introducing Akiho Shinomoto!

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:22.830
The curls in her hair are cute, 
and she's a great singer.

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:26.200
She's lived in England, Italy, Germany, 
France, Hong Kong, and now, Japan.

00:24:26.200 --> 00:24:28.120
She's only learned the formal 
Japanese speech style.

00:24:28.120 --> 00:24:30.580
She speaks super politely to everyone.

00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:32.910
What do ya call someone who speaks 
lots of languages, again?

00:24:32.910 --> 00:24:34.590
Uh, bilin... Er, violin?

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:34.200
<b>Multilingual</b>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:34.590 --> 00:24:38.360
But no one can beat me at the Kansai dialect! 
Boy, there's no stoppin' me!

00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.750
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.750
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.420 --> 00:24:43.390
As Meiling-chan and I were heading 
home from Tomoyo-chan's house,

00:24:43.390 --> 00:24:46.020
we ran into a girl wearing Chinese clothes.

00:24:46.020 --> 00:24:48.430
Could she be a card, too?

00:24:48.750 --> 00:24:51.750
Next time, "Sakura and Meiling's Friend."

00:24:48.750 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and Meiling's Friend</b>

00:24:51.750 --> 00:24:54.710
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
